      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1089,
          "quote": "The source\nlink identifies its authority; the interpreted predicate and derivation\njustify what the assertion can establish. Execution provenance identifies the\nactual subject, checker, environment, observations and result. Preserve these\nrelations in the existing ticket or evidence carrier, including shared\nderivations; no per-test ticket or duplicate provenance ledger follows.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#Ticket%20Method%2FTicket%20Rules%2FTest%20Case%20Authority",
          "start_line": 1084
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1096,
          "quote": "An acceptance predicate also needs an applicable supported entry or state and\nan obligation under the governing operating/threat model. Existing test presence\ncannot authorize an excluded threat or retain a superseded guard. Audit the\naffected predicates when changing that responsibility; retire unsupported\nexpectations under the owning basis without inventing a replacement guard.\nAn actual conflict in live authority requires re-entry, not a test-only waiver.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#Ticket%20Method%2FTicket%20Rules%2FTest%20Case%20Authority",
          "start_line": 1091
        }
      ],
      "key": "test_authority_and_provenance_rule",
      "statement": "Every substantive test case should derive through ticket → intake triage → lawful re-entry → governing requirement/design/module/graph/carrier/closure surface → expectation. This is a recommendation. Tests do not derive authority from current implementation. Apply parallel assurance separately to expectation derivation and executed checks: authority link, interpreted predicate and derivation establish assertion reach; execution provenance identifies actual subject, checker, environment, observations and result. Preserve shared derivations and these relations in existing ticket/evidence carriers without requiring per-test tickets or duplicate ledgers. Acceptance predicates additionally require supported applicable entry/state and an obligation under the governing operating/threat model. Existing tests cannot authorize excluded threats or retain superseded guards. Responsibility changes require predicate audit and retirement of unsupported expectations under their owning basis, without invented replacement guards. Live authority conflict requires re-entry, not a test-only waiver.",
      "uncertainty": "The referenced Foundations assurance contract is not supplied."
