      "conditions": [
        "A fixed ticket produces a mismatch between implementation behavior and test expectation"
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1114,
          "quote": "When a ticket is fixed and a mismatch appears between implementation behavior\nand test expectation, review must reconcile the mismatch in this order:\n\n1. the ticket's `change_intent`, `change_class`, `re_entry_point`,\n   `target_truth`, `superseded_truth`, `closure_law`,\n   `evaluation_criteria`, and `non_closure_conditions`\n2. the ticket's intake triage and lawful owning re-entry\n3. the governing requirement, design, module, graph-function, carrier, or\n   other cited authority surface\n4. the test case expectation\n5. the implementation\n\nThe implementation may prove that a test is stale, incomplete, or too narrow,\nbut it cannot by itself authorize changing the expected result.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#Ticket%20Method%2FTicket%20Rules%2FTest%20Case%20Authority",
          "start_line": 1101
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1128,
          "quote": "If a test predates a lawful ticket repricing, update or remove the test only\nafter naming the governing ticket and the authority change that superseded the\nold expectation.\n\nIf the ticket is stale, ambiguous, or missing the authority needed to decide the\ntest expectation, the work must re-enter triage before either the code or test\nis treated as correct.\n\nA passing test is closure evidence only when the test expectation can be traced\nback to the admitted ticket and its governing authority chain.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#Ticket%20Method%2FTicket%20Rules%2FTest%20Case%20Authority",
          "start_line": 1119
        }
      ],
      "key": "test_mismatch_reconciliation",
      "statement": "Reconcile in order: ticket change_intent/change_class/re_entry_point/target_truth/superseded_truth/closure_law/evaluation_criteria/non_closure_conditions; intake triage and lawful owning re-entry; cited governing requirement/design/module/graph-function/carrier/other authority; expectation; implementation. Implementation is evidence and may prove a test stale, incomplete or narrow, but cannot alone authorize a changed expected result. Code-only test adjustment is a ticket-method defect. A test predating lawful repricing may be updated/removed only after naming the governing ticket and superseding authority change. Stale, ambiguous or insufficiently authorized tickets require triage before either code or test is treated as correct. Passing tests qualify as closure evidence only with expectation traceability to the admitted ticket and authority chain.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
