      "key": "migration_declaration_and_checklist",
      "statement": "Both an explicit declaration block and hard live-markdown checklist are mandatory ticket authority, providing minimum reviewer checks before accepting a concrete closure claim. Declare strategy, exact affected scope, every excluded/disjoint Product or compatibility scope and deterministic routing, old/superseded and new/authoritative truth paths, old/new producer and consumer sets, every derived projection/report/status/proof surface, and closure law. Minimum checklist names scope/exclusions/routing, old/new paths, new producers/consumers and projection/read-model surfaces; requires old authority removed/demoted inside scope, mixed-state behavior excluded as closure evidence, mixed old/new tests removed/repriced, recurrence checked against library surfaces, library usage and governing library/rationale declared, one tenant lifecycle per backlog/active ticket with suffixed sibling tickets when applicable, and ticket/Product wording and proof claims reconciled before closure. Required fields are migration_strategy and library_usage.",
