      "key": "migration_closure_boundaries",
      "statement": "Local completion cannot close an unexamined interface family. Closure is blocked while the old authoritative interface passes normal execution inside affected scope, subject to the explicit retained-compatibility exception. Old paths cannot remain silently authoritative; retained ones must be named compatibility rather than native truth and justified in the ticket, not inferred from code. Mixed green tests and proxy/partial implementations do not establish migration closure. If completed-ticket checked closure items prove false on the current tree, reopen or create an explicitly linked successor; false closure is a ticket-method defect.",
